From: Hoki local maintainers <code@lukasrieger.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gatt-client: bound discovery cleanup to the requested range

Service Changed discovery operates on a bounded handle range. If replacement
of a cached service requires clearing a conflicting entry, parsing sets
op->last to the newly discovered service end. Completion currently clears
from there through 0xffff, removing unrelated services above the changed
range. Bound trailing cleanup by op->end and op->start. Full database
discovery still covers the whole address space; the 0xffff sentinel remains
a no-op and cannot wrap around.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/src/shared/gatt-client.c
+++ b/src/shared/gatt-client.c
@@ -478,9 +478,10 @@
 		gatt_db_remove_service(op->client->db, attr);
 	}
 
-	/* Reset remaining range */
-	if (op->last != UINT16_MAX)
-		gatt_db_clear_range(op->client->db, op->last + 1, UINT16_MAX);
+	/* Only invalidate handles covered by this discovery operation. */
+	if (op->last < op->end)
+		gatt_db_clear_range(op->client->db,
+					MAX(op->start, op->last + 1), op->end);
 
 	op->complete_func(op, success, err);
 }
